ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":91,"prev":93,"next":96,"titles":98,"firmware":24},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":25,"procedures":48,"parameters":49,"related":75,"body":79,"sources":80,"official_url":29,"controls":86},"fx.distortion","Distortion effect",[5,6,7,8,9],"distortion","overdrive","drive","clipping","dirt","fx",30,"knowledge/manual/units/fx/distortion.md",{"modes":14,"screens":16},[15],"auxiliary",[17],"M1","A clipping distortion for FX I or FX II; `M1` sets the drive into it, the clipping amount and low and high cuts that shape what enters it.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":24},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15","1.1.33",[26,32,35,40,45],{"id":27,"text":28,"source":29,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":31},"what","The distortion clips the signal it receives, adding grit and harmonics.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/fx#distorsion",null,"official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":29,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":31},"pre-filters","Low cut (`E3`) and high cut (`E4`) act on the input, trimming bass and treble before the clipping rather than after it.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":24,"confidence":39},"labels","The unit lists the effect as dist, and its columns read drive, clip, lo cut and hi cut — the guide's amount is labelled clip.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#213-auxiliary-tracks","verified",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":43,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":44},"start-values","A distortion page opens on drive 06, clip 99, lo cut 50 and hi cut 99 (one video, OS 1.0, the first second of the page).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":43,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":44},"hi-cut-open","High cut at 99 is open, since the pad kept its treble up to about 16 kHz through the distortion at the start values; the cut closes toward about 400 Hz as it goes to 0 (one video, OS 1.0, third-octave levels).",[],[50,57,63,69],{"screen":17,"encoder":51,"layer":52,"keys":53,"name":7,"range":30,"default":30,"cc":54,"cc_confidence":55,"note":56,"source":29,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":31},"E1","base","turn E1",12,"community-verified","level going into the distortion",{"screen":17,"encoder":58,"layer":52,"keys":59,"name":60,"range":30,"default":30,"cc":61,"cc_confidence":55,"note":62,"source":38,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":24,"confidence":39},"E2","turn E2","clip",13,"how hard the signal is clipped; the guide calls it amount",{"screen":17,"encoder":64,"layer":52,"keys":65,"name":66,"range":30,"default":30,"cc":67,"cc_confidence":55,"note":68,"source":29,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":31},"E3","turn E3","low cut",14,"how much bass reaches the distortion",{"screen":17,"encoder":70,"layer":52,"keys":71,"name":72,"range":30,"default":30,"cc":73,"cc_confidence":55,"note":74,"source":29,"firmware_min":30,"verified_on":30,"confidence":31},"E4","turn E4","high cut",15,"how much treble reaches the distortion",[76,77,78],"fx.overview","fx.lofi","mix.saturator","Drive sets how hot the signal hits the distortion, clip how hard it is clipped. Because the two\ncuts sit in front of the clipping, trimming the lows keeps bass from turning to mud, and trimming\nthe highs gives a darker, smoother crunch. As a send, it lets you add dirt to a drum bus or a lead\nby degrees while the dry track stays clean.",[81,83,85],{"url":29,"kind":82},"guide",{"url":38,"kind":84},"research",{"url":43,"kind":84},[87,88,89,90],"encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":10,"title":92},"Effects",{"id":94,"title":95},"fx.delay","Delay effect",{"id":77,"title":97},"Lofi effect",{"basics.key-notation":99,"basics.main-modes":100,"basics.modules":101,"basics.track-buttons":102,"basics.linked-tracks":103,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":104,"basics.workflow":105,"